menu "sys_device"

    config SYS_DEVICE_TYPES
        int "Device types"
        default 32
        range 1 64
        help
          Driver types this firmware registers (SYS_DEVICE_TYPE_DEFINE).

    config SYS_DEVICE_INTERCEPTORS
        int "Interceptors"
        default 2
        range 1 8
        help
          Contracts that can have an interceptor (sys_device_set_interceptor):
          a module that sees every call of the contract's ops before the
          device does (the power manager on POWER_VREG).

    config SYS_DEVICE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Wait for a device's lock (ms)"
        default 500
        range 100 60000
        help
          The longest a call waits for the lock of its device before it fails
          with ERR_DEV_BUSY (the op that holds the lock is in the error), so
          one device that hangs does not hold up the tasks that call it for
          good (the timers' task, the event task, a sweep). Longer than the
          slowest op of a device that runs under its lock (50 ms per I2C
          transfer; long ops like I2C SCAN use SYS_DEVICE_OP_NOLOCK).

    config SYS_DEVICE_EVENT_HOLD_BYTES
        int "Events held during a call (bytes)"
        default 256
        range 32 2048
        help
          Room for the events published inside device ops, kept until the
          task's outermost sys_device_call is over and then delivered to the
          inline listeners. On the stack of the task that makes that call,
          only while it runs. An event takes 4 B, its 20 B header and its
          payload, padded to 4 B; one that does not fit goes to the event
          task. A multiple of 4.

endmenu
